  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653. The RNA-only space is well-characterized: scvi_n200 + multiprofile dominates, and no remaining RNA-only config (config_004, 008, 009) is likely to exceed 0.653. The critical unexplored question is whether multimodal fusion can beat this baseline. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), so the key risk is that image features dilute the strong RNA signal. Config_033 pairs the best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) with resnet50 and uses weighted fusion, which can downweight the weaker image modality. This is the most informative single test: if it beats 0.653, multimodal is viable and we can refine with imagenet_vit_l in the final experiment; if it does not, we gain strong evidence that image adds no value here and we can confirm the RNA-only result as final. Testing resnet50 first (over imagenet_vit_l) is preferred because we already have a resnet50 baseline for interpreting the fusion effect."
}

